oxidebsd.org

Plain HTML and CSS, put together by build.sh and man.sh (POSIX sh) and a Makefile.

	make			build the site into _site/
	make man OXDOC=... MANDIR=...
				add the manual pages, rendered with oxdoc(1) from
				OxideBSD's share/man (OXDOC can be liboxdoc's oxdoc-host)
	make todo		list text still to be written
	make clean

.github/workflows/website.yml builds and deploys it to GitHub Pages on a push that changes
website/, once a day (for manual page changes in OxideBSD), and on demand.

Layout:

	pages/NAME.html		a page, at /NAME.html
	news/YYYY-MM-DD-slug.html
				a news post; listed on /news/ and in /news/atom.xml
	images/			copied as it is: the logo and icons (favicon.ico sits
				next to this file, since browsers ask for it at the root)
	template/		the header and footer around every page
	style.css
	CNAME			the domain, for GitHub Pages

A page or post is an HTML fragment whose first line is its title:

	<!-- title: What happened -->
	<p>...</p>

A "<!-- WRITE: ... -->" comment marks text still to be written; it doesn't show on the site.

The logo's lettering is black, which disappears in dark mode. A variant for it goes in
images/logo-dark.png, and template/head.html then picks it with
	<picture><source srcset="@ROOT@images/logo-dark.png" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
around the logo's img.
